# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this, a checkout is not byte-identical across machines: with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) the working tree gets CRLF while the
# repository stores LF, so any published sha256 of a working-tree file only
# reproduces on one platform. Declaring eol=lf makes the checkout deterministic
# everywhere. The stored blobs are already LF, so this changes no content.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
